From 8646fb567362650fe1f6396037f023d7508f05a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:56:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] fix(deploy): make the compose topology runnable

The compose file described a target topology that could not start:
the control plane image had no Dockerfile, the gateway was configured
through FORGEMESH_UPSTREAM although it reads GATEWAY_UPSTREAM_URL,
port 8000 was published while the gateway listens on 8081, the control
plane waited for a PostgreSQL server it does not use and its SQLite
database was not on a volume.

Both services now build from the new Dockerfiles. The database lives
on the control-plane-data volume, both services read the API key file
deploy/docker/api-keys.json as a compose secret (ignored by git), run
with a read-only root file system and without capabilities, and are
published on 127.0.0.1 only. The gateway starts once the control
plane reports ready on /readyz. PostgreSQL moved to the optional
"postgres" profile.

scripts/compose_smoke.sh builds the images, starts the stack and
checks through the gateway that requests without a key are rejected,
that a service can be created and read, that the controller writes
its status and that it survives a control plane restart.
